#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197987 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/id #uuid "88848c23-66fe-5937-958c-28d73b593d99" :question/math-academy-id "e-12487" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\nI_y = \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $\\mathcal{A} =  3\\cdot 1 = 3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}9\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3M[y]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =3M(2-1) \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nR_y^2 =\\dfrac{3M}{M} =  3\\quad \\Rightarrow\\quad R_y = \\sqrt{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197989 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "fa3e8249-cb9f-50f6-a56f-6f311d101de6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12495" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies one-half of the circle $x^2+y^2\\leq 1$ for $y\\geq 0.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda(x,y)=\\dfrac{3}{2}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\nI_0 = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda(r,\\theta) r^3 \\:\\textrm{d}r\\:\\textrm{d}\\theta,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(r,\\theta)$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda(r,\\theta)=\\dfrac{3}{2}Mr\\sin\\theta.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M({\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197991 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/id #uuid "5245b67a-8beb-512d-b3c8-2d38db797703" :question/math-academy-id "e-12507" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the lines $y = x,$ $x = 1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda(x,y) = 3Mx.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\nI_0 = \\iint\\limits_D (x^2 + y^2) \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq x \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 3Mx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{[\\frac{4}{15}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3M\\cdot \\frac{4}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b02d9443-7864-5741-b395-c24abbd2b736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194370} {:answer/id #uuid "d11dee5f-f185-5b9b-85b7-29b8b08efaa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194371} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d1d883-ab40-5185-ad71-55d14ca345ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194372} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff3388e-32ae-523f-9c3f-7f1f093b9f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194373} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbd58b5-99a0-5f3a-a047-c107325e40e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d11dee5f-f185-5b9b-85b7-29b8b08efaa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194371} :answer-field/id #uuid "abd0743b-879f-59db-972f-80ec21ea6912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e1eb104-83e6-5dc7-913b-3996107f92c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163011" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{4}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(4+9-(\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(13-\\frac{5}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{34}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{17}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16494fe4-d0ed-5f9c-bed6-a00ea02f1647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379911} {:answer/id #uuid "b2308161-7961-54e0-a175-1d02b5e1aa3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379912} {:answer/id #uuid "19e195af-fc39-5744-bea0-e0dfe05792ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379913} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6eb1e4-6d89-5179-b695-8fc60b311301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379914} {:answer/id #uuid "049c5f8f-16ae-5f59-9cd8-46a039bd11ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "049c5f8f-16ae-5f59-9cd8-46a039bd11ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379915} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd1f937-5a53-5b87-ad77-857d9f4b220d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42754aea-7d8d-54b5-837e-0461d25b662a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163576" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 3=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(8-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}[y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd1d861d-70b1-5f94-878c-cdf0c652497e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379918} {:answer/id #uuid "d27b8a24-f2c9-5eae-aa95-162fdb0c61b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379919} {:answer/id #uuid "278ade40-aa05-53fd-bb03-5ece8bfbeb8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379920} {:answer/id #uuid "b20ccb8a-7acc-55e8-bab1-a75ab00e14fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379921} {:answer/id #uuid "b89dde50-0f9e-5a7a-a380-c941f631bb7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d27b8a24-f2c9-5eae-aa95-162fdb0c61b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379919} :answer-field/id #uuid "09a3c335-ab68-54bb-a924-2f3f97a04c7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f102fc37-9019-5b5f-8138-fd88fa02f824" :question/math-academy-id "q-163578" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 3=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(1+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{10M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65672802-b56e-5cdf-b448-d67b8fc900ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379925} {:answer/id #uuid "30c949c4-7a2f-5a4e-89ac-3056df09c554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379926} {:answer/id #uuid "c9216752-f02e-5757-895c-ba8a27a5f3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379927} {:answer/id #uuid "7fef4efd-1624-5b4d-aacc-9546dc541e13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379928} {:answer/id #uuid "09b0ee51-fd2f-55b3-af7a-877e2a3322b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fef4efd-1624-5b4d-aacc-9546dc541e13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379928} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd246c4e-734a-579c-b7b6-4603ef46836e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ac58438-3de5-5bce-96c1-06b2a8754602" :question/math-academy-id "q-163582" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{7}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{7}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(7+9-\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{40}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{20}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{20}{3}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc8c3d1-413d-544b-9266-8cc15bf82ccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379932} {:answer/id #uuid "53086998-2c28-53ca-9caa-cf03493be237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379933} {:answer/id #uuid "552ec8db-ab66-5495-912a-a61bbcf5c11b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379934} {:answer/id #uuid "629729fa-bbe3-5f4a-960b-a75563f95ecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379935} {:answer/id #uuid "6fea5c47-7dca-52ef-80db-584acd1cd454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "629729fa-bbe3-5f4a-960b-a75563f95ecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379935} :answer-field/id #uuid "85e903b2-e31d-50b2-afca-dfb20dadf9b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "41711bc6-3248-5171-a778-081733948b48" :question/math-academy-id "q-163594" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 3.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{x}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}\\theta -\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63216723-86dd-5ed7-b0c3-effa279969ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379939} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb0cefe-1946-5d9f-8d93-4684d174f423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379940} {:answer/id #uuid "d20cdaab-47a4-5b36-8b23-0d8606eb9626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379941} {:answer/id #uuid "729cda97-28b4-5e75-b396-d85ea0629325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379942} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe74375-008e-5747-8c6a-9cde25c80c2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "729cda97-28b4-5e75-b396-d85ea0629325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379942} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8f84ea-33ea-5ed0-8e57-33764b41f2fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b75f6b7-1feb-5cd3-b6ce-f7c0075a6bc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-163600" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ the line $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=12Mxy.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 12Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}{x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}]}_{y=\\sqrt{x}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}x)-(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =12M(\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =12M\\cdot \\frac{7}{80} \\\\  & =\\frac{21M}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21M}{20}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cacc079-86bb-5220-a40f-8de5c9b8e07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194448} {:answer/id #uuid "d79108fb-d801-52ba-9648-47fa212c3fe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194449} {:answer/id #uuid "41c4018b-c4f8-57ea-bd03-fc8883e007ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194450} {:answer/id #uuid "4d75ca10-6598-54e6-af76-86b267fba7bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194451} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9ef8a1-d1a7-5488-b4b2-2cc2dda43c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c4018b-c4f8-57ea-bd03-fc8883e007ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194450} :answer-field/id #uuid "367d03c1-12cd-5b35-bf55-9c5e6d150f37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3adab878-1dd3-5ac8-88b6-a5059624907c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163604" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the lines $y=x,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{4}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{5}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb74736a-8d0b-5c05-9cf5-572efeafc18c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194454} {:answer/id #uuid "e92bea8e-f329-5746-8ac2-7ca8ac92e5c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194455} {:answer/id #uuid "ec16a955-c293-52d9-af32-02c5eebae5b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194456} {:answer/id #uuid "70f36d0e-2e40-5444-aad5-8a1e28af0485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194457} {:answer/id #uuid "72af5f2b-9243-5236-b032-56821da7f649" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e92bea8e-f329-5746-8ac2-7ca8ac92e5c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194455} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a506e94-1bce-5e06-a39e-3ad89a824e57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2496e287-b250-5877-a40c-af954399de62" :question/math-academy-id "q-163612" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\frac{1}{3}(1-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}[y]_{4}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(6-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c99e2c5c-421a-55ee-ada2-296ef7391ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379946} {:answer/id #uuid "60f521be-731f-5cf8-a200-ca375ca4d946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379947} {:answer/id #uuid "a6781a22-1d4d-5f1e-9a19-8b0f30cdd4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379948} {:answer/id #uuid "c68a1e04-3a57-5761-9388-b1fc7725f6a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379949} {:answer/id #uuid "9a181cf5-af1f-51c2-9ade-207f5eccd245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6781a22-1d4d-5f1e-9a19-8b0f30cdd4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379948} :answer-field/id #uuid "da0954a8-5ca4-5af1-ba8e-132189df6306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afafc33f-cb3e-5594-b630-d8df16a9a255" :question/math-academy-id "q-163614" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y={x}^{2}.$ Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=20Mx.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{{x}^{2}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 20Mx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =20M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{{x}^{2}}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =20M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y={x}^{3}}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{7}-{x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{8}-\\frac{1}{11}{x}^{11}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}(\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{11}) \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{88} \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5M}{22}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{22}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62463465-16ae-52e2-b1ad-3819c738909f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379953} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef513dd-a601-5bcc-abf7-45c89edbb091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{67}{60}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379954} {:answer/id #uuid "f5eb56e5-70bf-5f9a-b83c-37be34b75d59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{52}{41}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379955} {:answer/id #uuid "61a26b23-b857-5874-9afe-162898090845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{93}{70}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379956} {:answer/id #uuid "edf2cee5-b9f7-5ce9-9087-ff275f94b555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61a26b23-b857-5874-9afe-162898090845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{93}{70}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379956} :answer-field/id #uuid "4399627a-a895-52a7-a0ea-7efa0df9ce90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5a55592d-e97d-5673-88f1-e39a7437cfff" :question/math-academy-id "q-163645" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies region bounded by two circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{14\\pi }M\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{14\\pi }Mr.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{14\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{93M}{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{93M}{70}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{93}{70}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1782786-c99e-5706-95f4-e348e16fd5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379960} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e5cc8b-2506-50d2-afa5-32fc1168679d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379961} {:answer/id #uuid "99b42a1f-ecf9-5bfd-b64d-391a6c4b210b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379962} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6ac81d-a1a8-5904-9aaa-112cd57680b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379963} {:answer/id #uuid "ef045a0f-cfe3-5ab9-aa0e-cdbd03c3cacf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef045a0f-cfe3-5ab9-aa0e-cdbd03c3cacf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379964} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a73b21b-8693-53c9-b09c-068d274ba5bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9acf39a4-64d3-553b-9958-8b97a070f182" :question/math-academy-id "q-163650" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2$ for $x\\ge 0.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2M}{\\pi }{y}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{2M}{\\pi }{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}{sin}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{4}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{(\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +1}{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{3}{8}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot {[\\frac{3\\theta }{8}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }{32}]}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{8} \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a08c0d15-519b-5833-bf89-f478d5d65d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379967} {:answer/id #uuid "f81728d3-164e-5677-af8f-f16be9f2feda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379968} {:answer/id #uuid "92674799-0b41-5422-bd97-ecc681558abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379969} {:answer/id #uuid "6165bbc0-de39-5bec-a731-cc429253e058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379970} {:answer/id #uuid "f00fffb7-fa7b-5270-b6a6-58859f3f4cfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92674799-0b41-5422-bd97-ecc681558abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379969} :answer-field/id #uuid "c705de2f-b369-5420-971d-96cd88370316" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a99d2798-c187-5104-9954-2eb7a502ad0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163657" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region between two circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{x}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{1}^{2}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{21}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e85e81b-786d-5ded-91f5-48bb4b426e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379974} {:answer/id #uuid "3784ab27-6817-5e75-8e03-9660a1438e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379975} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f9408f-b5d3-5184-99e4-9a5849d63deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379976} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c0c337-87a6-5635-9897-82b1a4b66684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379977} {:answer/id #uuid "3348d404-dbb8-53ce-9c39-aeaa55ab74cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{7\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3348d404-dbb8-53ce-9c39-aeaa55ab74cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{7\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379978} :answer-field/id #uuid "71d41b46-cece-5da6-8f82-a66347a43318" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d6194c5-1762-5426-8143-928d732b6bf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-38820" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2},$ the line $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{20M}{7}(x+y).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{20M}{7}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{[\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{14}{x}^{7}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{14}) \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}\\cdot \\frac{5}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{100M}{147}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{100M}{147}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{100}{147}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{7\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddb21c70-1481-5a92-8fc2-1b177953f280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197534} {:answer/id #uuid "e068f940-7aac-5622-a982-fea1fcf70d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{70}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197535} {:answer/id #uuid "17201259-2269-51dc-b19d-d13dbe0e4369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197536} {:answer/id #uuid "39f6ab5b-7b4c-55a2-a62c-1ac671ddb033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197537} {:answer/id #uuid "6454bd2a-6c85-555a-9760-fa966a1a906e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6454bd2a-6c85-555a-9760-fa966a1a906e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197538} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1126568-932c-58b6-b4b4-662b05e697a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2db88b84-fe57-56b2-8d78-b4ac01dd1164" :question/math-academy-id "q-38824" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $x={y}^{2}.$ Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=12Mxy.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 12Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}12x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}[3x{y}^{4}]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{10}{x}^{10}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =M(\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{3}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9M}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9M}{20}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d63eec45-6603-524b-8b1d-8cafe4400294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197540} {:answer/id #uuid "1c216982-e507-5c04-8510-d5cf017c3e1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197541} {:answer/id #uuid "456ccd78-2fa8-5537-8f57-f080774e1a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197542} {:answer/id #uuid "614ef90a-009d-574b-b93b-7cbd61d3ff5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197543} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0e82f2-9239-5d13-a910-b57f9213ac92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c216982-e507-5c04-8510-d5cf017c3e1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197541} :answer-field/id #uuid "043793c1-378d-5a98-85c7-52b59096096c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b6fbab0f-40fd-5c65-87d5-1b56f0245d59" :question/math-academy-id "q-38825" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4$ in the first quadrant. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{8}Mx.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{8}Mr\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M({\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}(1-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{8M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
